      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Slight necro post, but yes.\nEspecially with the advent of Contacts and being able to pull data from Physbones, it's not hard to have the FX layer absolutely BALLOON (Because lets be honest, FX is the only layer that actually matters for 90% of custom avatar things). Plus the fact most of anything actually useful ends up needing to be in the FX layer, it makes it more of a pain to split up setups and make them transportable. For some examples, having a pre-made \"Face Tracking\" or \"Haptics\" animator that gets passed around that you can slap onto anything with some light editing, while keeping your custom things untouched, would be amazing for organization and for updating specific things by way of just removing the one animator instead of digging into a single master FX animator to change things.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
